<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Written out in full rather than inheriting a vanilla abstract recipe. The mech gestation
    bases do exist (Vanilla Factions Expanded uses MediumMechanoidRecipe and
    HeavyMechanoidRecipe), but inheriting one would silently pull in that tier's ingredients,
    research and gestator - and this recipe is deliberately unlike any of them: no subcore.

    Three fields carry the whole gestator contract, and all three are load-bearing:

      gestationCycles > 0   is what makes BillUtility.MakeNewBill hand back a Bill_ProductionMech
                            instead of a plain Bill_Production. Building_MechGestator.Tick casts
                            its active bill to Bill_Mech unconditionally, so a bill of any other
                            class on that table is a null reference on the next tick.

      products              must name a PAWN ThingDef. Bill_ProductionMech.CreateProducts looks
                            up the PawnKindDef whose race is this def and generates it, and
                            Notify_FormingCompleted casts the result to Pawn and reads its
                            kindDef. An item product would be a null reference there.

      mechanitorOnlyRecipe  keeps non-mechanitors out. Bill_Mech.PawnAllowedToStartAnew calls
                            p.mechanitor.HasBandwidthForBill, and p.mechanitor is null for
                            anyone without a mechlink; the base class's mechanitorOnlyRecipe
                            check runs first and returns false, which is what stops that being
                            a null reference. Vanilla's own mech recipes all set it.

    So gestating a Riimba needs a mechanitor, same as any mech. It costs that mechanitor no
    bandwidth once built, because the unit's BandwidthCost stat is 0 and its orders come from a
    control station instead - see Riimba.xml.
  -->

  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>Riimba_Gestate</defName>
    <label>gestate riimba</label>
    <description>Gestate a Riimba cleaning drone. Unlike a combat mech it carries no subcore of its own - the thinking is done by the control station that drives it, so a drone gestated with no station built is an expensive paperweight until one is.</description>
    <jobString>Gestating a riimba.</jobString>
    <workAmount>800</workAmount>
    <!-- One cycle at half a day. A Riimba is the cheapest thing the gestator can make. -->
    <gestationCycles>1</gestationCycles>
    <formingTicks>30000</formingTicks>
    <mechanitorOnlyRecipe>true</mechanitorOnlyRecipe>
    <researchPrerequisite>RiimbaCleaning</researchPrerequisite>
    <recipeUsers>
      <li>MechGestator</li>
    </recipeUsers>
    <ingredients>
      <li>
        <filter>
          <thingDefs>
            <li>Steel</li>
          </thingDefs>
        </filter>
        <count>60</count>
      </li>
      <li>
        <filter>
          <thingDefs>
            <li>ComponentIndustrial</li>
          </thingDefs>
        </filter>
        <count>3</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <fixedIngredientFilter>
      <thingDefs>
        <li>Steel</li>
        <li>ComponentIndustrial</li>
      </thingDefs>
    </fixedIngredientFilter>
    <products>
      <Riimba>1</Riimba>
    </products>
    <descriptionHyperlinks>
      <ThingDef>Riimba</ThingDef>
    </descriptionHyperlinks>
  </RecipeDef>

</Defs>
